### Goal Model Decomposition

The mission is decomposed into a hierarchical goal model that captures the delivery of food and the retrieval of dirty dishes in a hospital setting. The model uses AND and OR decompositions to represent the necessary tasks and their relationships.

### Goal Model Table

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Goal Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|--------------------|-----------|-----------|---------------|
| G1      | Provide Food and Dish Services | Provide food and dish services to inpatients. | ; (sequential) | Achieve | - | Both food delivery and dish retrieval are required, hence sequential execution. |
| G2      | Food Delivery Service | Deliver food from the kitchen to inpatient rooms. | # (parallel) | Perform | AND | G1 requires both food delivery and dish retrieval, hence AND with G3. |
| G3      | Dish Retrieval Service | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient rooms. | # (parallel) | Perform | AND | G1 requires both food delivery and dish retrieval, hence AND with G2. |
| G2.1    | Direct Delivery | Deliver food directly using a special manipulation skill. | - | Perform | OR | Alternative method for food delivery. |
| G2.2    | Tray Fetching | Deliver food via tray, requiring cooperation. | - | Perform | OR | Alternative method for food delivery. |
| G2.2.1  | Inpatient Fetch | Inpatient retrieves food from the tray. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible cooperation methods. |
| G2.2.2  | Companion Fetch | Companion retrieves food from the tray. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible cooperation methods. |
| G2.2.3  | Nurse Fetch | Nurse retrieves food from the tray. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible cooperation methods. |
| G2.2.4  | Robot Fetch | Another robot retrieves food from the tray. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible cooperation methods. |
| G3.1    | Unassisted Dish Retrieval | Retrieve dishes without assistance. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible dish retrieval methods. |
| G3.2    | Robot Cooperation | Retrieve dishes with another robot. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible dish retrieval methods. |
| G3.3    | Human Signal | Retrieve dishes when signaled by a human. | - | Perform | OR | One of the possible dish retrieval methods. |

### Task Model Table

| Task ID | Task Title | Task Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|-----------|-----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT2.1   | Direct Delivery | Robot delivers food directly. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Requires one robot with special skills. |
| AT2.2   | Tray Fetching | Retrieve food from tray with cooperation. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | May involve a human or another robot. |
| AT3.1   | Unassisted Retrieval | Retrieve dishes without help. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Robot can do this alone. |
| AT3.2   | Robot Cooperation | Two robots retrieve dishes. | AND | Hospital room | 2 | Requires two robots for heavy loads. |
| AT3.3   | Human Signal | Retrieve dishes when signaled. | AND | Hospital room | 1 | Robot responds to human signal. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are required, so they must both succeed.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either direct delivery or tray fetching can be used.

- **G2.2 -> G2.2.1, G2.2.2, G2.2.3, G2.2.4 [OR]**  
  Justification: Any of the cooperation methods can fulfill tray fetching.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2, G3.3 [OR]**  
  Justification: Any retrieval method can be used.

- **G2 -> AT2.1, AT2.2 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both tasks are part of the food delivery process.

- **G3 -> AT3.1, AT3.2, AT3.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both tasks are part of the dish retrieval process.

This model ensures that the system can handle various scenarios efficiently, leveraging both robot capabilities and human cooperation when necessary.
